  "body": "It's currently impossible to draw repeating/mirrored gradients (at least, in a single call) in Canvas2D.\r\n\r\n- CSS [supports](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-images-3/#funcdef-repeating-radial-gradient) repeating gradients\r\n- SVG [supports](https://www.w3.org/Graphics/SVG/1.1/pservers.html#LinearGradientSpreadMethodAttribute) repeating/mirrored gradients\r\n- The COLR (version 1) table in OpenType [supports](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/typography/opentype/spec/colr#color-lines) repeating/mirrored gradients\r\n- Someone on Stack Overflow is [asking](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/56398519/how-to-make-a-repeating-canvasgradient) for repeating gradients\r\n\r\nRepeating/mirrored gradients seem like a useful and natural addition to canvas 2d.\r\n\r\nPolyfilling repeating gradients (by drawing individual gradients in a loop) isn't possible, because some radial repeating gradients actually fit infinite periods into finite space:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"300\" alt=\"Screenshot 2022-08-20 at 11 29 28 PM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/918903/186082001-59e8cf1b-dfc3-4663-ae66-0e12e7111d1b.png\">\r\n",
